=== layout: one-panel

# Interpret the p-value

@body

- A chi-square statistic needs its degrees of freedom.
- The p-value is a right-tail probability under H~0~.
- Small p: this much disagreement, or more, is unusual under H~0~.
- Large p: insufficient evidence to reject H~0~.
- p is not the probability that H~0~ is true.

Here: &chi;^2^ &asymp; 0.178, df = 3, p &asymp; 0.981.

=== layout: one-panel

# df = 3: locate the critical value

@body

| Right-tail p | 0.10 | 0.05 | 0.01 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Critical chi-square | 6.251 | 7.815 | 11.345 |

@notes

At alpha = 0.05, the critical value is 7.815 (about 7.82).

=== layout: one-panel

# Compare with the critical value

@body

- df = 3; &alpha; = 0.05
- Critical value &asymp; 7.82

*&chi;^2^ = 0.178 < 7.82: fail to reject H~0~.*

The counts do not provide sufficient evidence against the proposed ratio.

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# Why use a table?

@body

- The exact p-value comes from a tail area, not simple arithmetic.
- For statistic x and df = k, integrate t^(k/2 - 1)^ e^(-t)^:
  - numerator: from x/2 to infinity
  - denominator: from 0 to infinity
- Divide numerator by denominator.

Use the chi-square table or software for the calculation.

@notes

The source stacked integral equation cannot be faithfully represented by the native Djot math subset. The explanatory draft remains editable underneath. Original StarMath:
F( %chi^2 , k ) ~=~
{`int from{%chi^2 / 2} to{infinity} x^{ {k over 2}`-1 } e^-x dx`}
over
{`int from{0} to{infinity} x^{ {k over 2}`-1 } e^-x dx`}


=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# The exact tail probability

@body

- x = 0.178; k = 3
- Lower limit in numerator: x/2 = 0.089
- Numerator &asymp; 0.869442
- Denominator &asymp; 0.886227

*p &asymp; 0.98106 > 0.05: fail to reject H~0~.*


@notes

The source stacked integral equation cannot be faithfully represented by the native Djot math subset. The explanatory draft remains editable underneath. Original StarMath:
F( %chi^2 , k ) ~=~
{`int from{%chi^2 / 2} to{infinity} x^{ {k over 2}`-1 } e^-x dx`}
over
{`int from{0} to{infinity} x^{ {k over 2}`-1 } e^-x dx`}
~=~
{`int from{0.178 / 2} to{infinity} x^{ {3 over 2}`-1 } e^-x dx`}
over
{`int from{0} to{infinity} x^{ {3 over 2}`-1 } e^-x dx`}

newline

~=~
{`0.869442`} over {`0.886227`} ~=~ 0.98106 ~>~ 0.05

